      en: "A large, shallow bay south of the Mayabeque province, part of the Gulf of Batabanó. Important wetland. Mouth of several small rivers. Shallow water depth. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Cuba, the Caribbean island nation, reflecting the interplay of history, tobacco and sugarcane cultivation, and tropical nature. Located in Cuba, the largest island state in the Caribbean. Tropical-humid climate with distinct wet and dry seasons. Havana, the capital, is the country's political and cultural hub."
